comparing total reads:

```{r}
apply(original_submission,2,sum)
apply(rerun_ludo,2,sum)
apply(original_submission,2,sum)-apply(rerun_ludo,2,sum)
```
Minuscule variation, except for 10L2brain (7591-**36**-49-1).It looks like in Breana's case, 10L2Brain was not concatenated. I excluded that I concatenated twice by rerunning the concatenation and checking output size

That is the main difference between the two runs. The minor variation is weird but it could come from trinity itself. One could simply run it with the half of data for 10L2 brain that Breana got (once we figure which one that is) if we wanted to keep going with that analysis.

    

